                         MAIL DROP FAQ - Ver. 0.9


What is a Mail Drop?

We don't call them mail drops.  We also don't call them P.O. Boxes.  We
call them Mail Receiving Services in the US or Accomodation Addresses
in Europe.  A Mail Receiving Service is a business that provides you with
an address where you can receive postal mail and package deliveries from
the commercial package delivery services.  Many Mail Receiving Services
also offer other services such as telephone answering (conventional or
voice mail), facsimile, packing and shipping, and general business/office
services.
 

